# Hub API (Afterglow)

The Hub REST contract lives in the sibling repo:

`../avn-hub/openapi/openapi.yaml`

(or `C:/Users/Watak/Documents/GitHub/avn-hub/openapi/openapi.yaml` if needed).

Before adding Hub client methods or changing request/response models in `Afterglow.HubClient` / `Afterglow.Core.Models`, read that OpenAPI file.

Catalog browse/search returns `CatalogPage` (`items`, `page`, `total_pages`, `rows`, `has_more`), not a bare array. Preview uses `GET /api/v1/catalog/preview`.

Screenshot galleries: prefer `cached_url`; uncached items still appear via `full_url`. Refresh may take up to ~120s while the hub caches images/GIFs.

Notable game tracking fields (`PATCH /api/v1/games/{id}`):

- `play_status`: `unplayed` | `playing` | `completed` | `dropped`
- `user_rating`: omit unchanged; JSON `null` clears; number sets (half-stars 0.5–5)
- `user_notes`: string

Download links (`GET /api/v1/games/{id}/download-links`):

- `label` — platform (Windows, Linux, PC, …)
- `title` — pack/section heading above a hoster cluster (Episode 5, v0.4 Full, …) when the thread uses one
